ioquake3 for RISC OS
====================
Version 0.1.2 (1 Nov 2026)

Quake III Arena's engine (ioquake3), for RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi 2 or
later (best on a Pi 4). The 3D is drawn by the processor, with riscos-mesa's
OpenGL, so it runs at a low resolution scaled up to fill the screen.

Game data
---------
ioquake3 is the engine only. Put game data beside !RunImage, in this
application:

 - The free Quake III Arena demo: run !ioquake3 without any game data
   and it offers to download it. It fetches id's Linux demo installer
   (49 MB) from a mirror of id's FTP site, checks it, shows id's
   licence (kept as demoq3.Q3A_EULA/txt) and installs the demo's data
   (demoq3.pak0/pk3, 47 MB) only if you accept it, then starts the
   game. It needs about 100 MB free while it works. If the download
   fails, fetch linuxq3ademo-1.11-6.x86.gz.sh yourself (from
   ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/ftp.idsoftware.com/idstuff/quake3/linux) and
   drop it on the icon bar icon; or put pak0/pk3 from it in demoq3 by
   hand. demoq3.zz-ioq3-vm/pk3, already there, holds ioquake3's game
   code, which the demo's own is too old for.
 - The full game: make a baseq3 folder and put pak0/pk3 to pak8/pk3 in
   it. pak0 is on the CD, or buy the game from Steam or GOG (see
   ioquake3.org/buy); pak1 to pak8 are id's free point release data,
   from ioquake3.org/extras/patch-data.
 - OpenArena (free, openarena.ws): put the pk3 files from OpenArena
   0.8.8's baseoa folder in a baseoa folder here. It's slower than
   Quake III (its maps draw more): about 10 to 20 frames a second;
   r_renderHeight 240 helps.

!Run uses baseq3 if it's there, else baseoa, else demoq3.

You need SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (from PackMan). For sound,
SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager, or DigitalRenderer, in !System.

Playing
-------
Double-click !ioquake3. It starts full screen at the desktop's
resolution, drawing 300 lines on a Pi 4 (about 25 to 35 frames a second
with bots) or 200 on a slower Pi (a Pi 3: about 20), scaled up by the
Pi's display hardware (VideoOverlay).

With a GPU (!RISC3D with a driver: RoMac on a Mac, or a Pi 4's
V3DRender) it draws at the full size instead, with Quake's lightmaps
and smooth textures. The speed settings below are for drawing without
one; settings saved for one way move to the other's defaults when that
changes, except ones you've changed yourself.
The mouse turns; the keys are Quake's (Setup > Controls to change them).

Settings that matter for speed (in the console, or q3config.cfg):

  r_renderHeight 300   lines drawn (200 on a slower Pi; 240 is faster,
                       360 sharper;
                       0 draws at the full screen size: very slow)
  r_renderWidth 0      0: as wide as the screen's shape needs
  r_overlay 1          scale with the display hardware (VideoOverlay)
  r_vertexLight 1      lighting from the map's vertices, one pass per
                       surface. 0 gives Quake's lightmaps (better
                       looking, about half as fast)
  r_fastsky 1          a plain sky: about 12% faster
  r_textureMode GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_NEAREST
                       blockier textures: about 18% faster
  r_glFastest 1        keeps mipmapped textures on riscos-mesa's fast
                       path (3 times as fast as 0)
  r_ext_multitexture 0 two passes instead of two texture units, which
                       riscos-mesa does slowly (lightmaps and
                       OpenArena: 2 to 3 times as fast)
  r_skyLast 1          the sky drawn after the world, which hides most
                       of it (about 5% faster; 0 draws it first)
  r_sortDepth 32       the world drawn nearest first, in steps this many
                       units deep, so riscos-mesa skips texturing what
                       is hidden (about 2% faster; 0: by texture only)
  r_textureMode GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_NEAREST_LINEAR
                       distant textures from one texel, close ones
                       smoothed (about 9% faster than
                       GL_LINEAR_MIPMAP_NEAREST, which blends four;
                       GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_NEAREST is a further 4% but
                       blocky up close)

Each of these but the last three needs vid_restart (or a restart) to take
effect.

Windowed: r_fullscreen 0, r_mode -1, r_customwidth/r_customheight.

Files
-----
The console log, settings and screenshots go in the game's folder
(demoq3, baseoa or baseq3). stdout and stderr are in this application.

Source and licence
------------------
ioquake3 is GPL 2 (or later): the source, with the RISC OS changes, is
at the project's home. It uses riscos-mesa (Mesa, SDL2, OpenAL Soft:
MIT/zlib/LGPL) and UnixLib. Quake III Arena's data is id Software's and
isn't included.

